  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Agriculture</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Agriculture</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Development Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">L&apos;agriculture est la science et la pratique de la production de denr&#xe9;es alimentaires, d&apos;aliments pour animaux et de fibres (y compris la foresterie, la faune, la p&#xea;che, l&apos;aquaculture et la floriculture) et ses relations avec les ressources naturelles, la transformation, la commercialisation, la distribution, l&apos;utilisation (y compris la nutrition) et le commerce.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">L&#x2019;objectif primordial du programme RISE est d&#x2019;accro&#xee;tre la r&#xe9;silience aux chocs des populations chroniquement vuln&#xe9;rables dans les zones de moyens d&#x2019;existence agro-pastorales et agricoles marginales du Sahel. Le programme quinquennal est mis en &#x153;uvre dans des zones cibl&#xe9;es du Burkina Faso et du Niger en Afrique de l&apos;Ouest.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the youth development activity is to increase pathways for rural young people to improve their livelihoods in Senegals Feed the Future (FTF) zone of influence (ZOI) which includes includes the Senegal river valley, sine saloum, and the casamance. The activity targets agriculture, entrepreneurship, and leadership, and will provide both technical and social solutions to youth un- and underemployment. Through existing and new relationships with public and private institutions, such as incubators, training centers, universities (notably the centers for research and piloting), businesses, youth-dedicated and government-run programs, the activity will connect youth to technical expertise while helping these institutions provide high quality and relevant services to the community. This activity will prioritize youth residing in rural areas, who are largely outside of the formal education system. Private sector engagement will serve as a critical means for leveraging resources, sector specific know how, and insight into labor market dynamics.</narrative>
  </description>
